    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s roster on June 23, the strongest starts are anchored by a high-upside core facing favorable conditions. **Cal Raleigh** (68.07) is our premier play; while he faces a decent arm in Keller, the wind blowing out adds critical elevation potential to his power profile, pushing his efficiency well into the \"Strong\" tier. **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Matt Chapman** (65.92) also benefit from that same park environment against Civale. Even with a minor BvP tax on **Luis Arraez**, his leadoff spot in the order maximizes his opportunity to contribute across our categories, and **Matt Chapman** remains a high-floor selection despite the defensive adjustment for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range, where **Drew Gilbert** (54.48) was the last player left on the bench. He was considered for the final outfield slot, but ultimately, the depth of our lineup pushed him out; the optimizer preferred the superior matchup density for **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.84), who both command significant platoon advantages today. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Taylor Ward** closely; while both project as \"Strong\" starts based on their matchups against Johnson, their values are sensitive to their actual spot in the batting order. We are proceeding with **Taylor Ward** at the top of the lineup, but any shift into the bottom third would necessitate a re-evaluation of his daily efficiency score.",
